---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Pricing & Scope | USIVA';
const description = 'A plain-language guide to USIVA scope, planning categories, provider terms, and the questions to clarify before payment.';
const canonical = 'https://usiva.org/pricing.html';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  activePath="/pricing.html"
  canonical={canonical}
  topbarMessage="Scope before spend · verify terms and sources directly."
  topbarLink={{ label: 'Prepare a question brief', href: '/contacts.html' }}
>
  <section class="scope-intro" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <div class="shell-container scope-intro__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Pricing / a transparent answer</p>
        <h1 id="page-title">Start with scope before you discuss price.</h1>
        <p class="scope-intro__lede">USIVA public pages organize visa and immigration planning questions. A provider’s written scope, deliverables, terms, and current source checks establish the commercial conversation.</p>
        <nav class="intro-actions" aria-label="Scope next steps">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="/contacts.html">Ask for scope</a>
          <a class="button button--outline" href="/services.html">See planning coverage</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
      <aside class="scope-note" aria-labelledby="scope-note-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Scope first</p>
        <h2 id="scope-note-heading">The right number depends on the actual question.</h2>
        <p>Stage, documents, location, provider, timing, and the authority responsible for the decision all matter. Confirm those details directly before paying anyone.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="scope-heading">
    <div class="shell-container">
      <header class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What this page can establish</p>
        <h2 id="scope-heading">A scope conversation has four useful edges.</h2>
        <p>The rows below are planning categories for clarifying scope, deliverables, and the responsible decision owner.</p>
      </header>

      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table class="scope-table">
          <caption>Questions to clarify before paying for immigration-related work</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr><th scope="col">Planning edge</th><th scope="col">Question to clarify</th><th scope="col">What remains outside this page</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">01 · Orientation</th><td>What stage am I in, and which decision is actually next?</td><td>Eligibility, adjudication, or an individualized legal opinion.</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">02 · Document map</th><td>Which records, translations, dates, or instructions should I gather and verify?</td><td>A guarantee that a packet is complete or accepted.</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">03 · Pathway conversation</th><td>Which school, sponsor, employer, or government source owns the next answer?</td><td>Authority to issue a visa, status, employment authorization, or approval.</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">04 · Specialist handoff</th><td>What personal facts make licensed advice the responsible next step?</td><td>Representation, filing, or legal work by an unnamed provider.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--mist" aria-labelledby="payment-heading">
    <div class="shell-container payment-grid">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">Before any payment</p>
        <h2 id="payment-heading">Ask for the terms in writing.</h2>
        <p>A careful scope note identifies who is providing the work, what the reader will receive, the boundaries of that work, which dates and sources matter, and where individualized legal questions belong.</p>
      </header>

      <ol class="payment-list">
        <li><span>01</span><div><strong>Name the provider.</strong><p>Confirm the relationship directly with the provider named in the written terms.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>02</span><div><strong>Name the deliverable.</strong><p>Ask whether the work is education, document organization, a consultation, a filing service, or something else.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>03</span><div><strong>Name the boundary.</strong><p>Confirm which questions belong to the provider and which official instruction controls the next action.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>04</span><div><strong>Name the next check.</strong><p>Rules, school instructions, sponsor requirements, and fees can change; ask when the information was last verified.</p></div></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scope-faq" aria-labelledby="questions-heading">
    <div class="shell-container scope-faq__grid">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">Questions worth carrying</p>
        <h2 id="questions-heading">A price describes a service; the responsible authority determines the result.</h2>
        <p>Use these prompts to keep a commercial conversation separate from an immigration decision.</p>
      </header>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details open><summary>What does a payment cover?</summary><p>A payment covers the written deliverable and terms agreed with the provider. Admission, employment, funding, visa issuance, and government approval remain decisions of the responsible authority.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can a planning page tell me whether I qualify?</summary><p>General information can help you identify questions. A personal eligibility analysis belongs with the school, sponsor, government source, or licensed immigration attorney responsible for the matter.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How is a responsible amount established?</summary><p>A responsible amount follows a real scope and direct confirmation of the provider, deliverables, timing, and terms.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What should I do if a claim sounds too certain?</summary><p>Ask for the source, the date checked, the person or institution that controls the decision, and the written terms. Request an explanation before sending money or beginning an activity; confirm the facts, terms, and authority first.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section scope-next" aria-labelledby="next-heading">
    <div class="shell-container">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">Low-risk next steps</p>
        <h2 id="next-heading">Start with the question you need priced or verified.</h2>
        <p>Prepare a short brief, then confirm the right destination and written terms before payment.</p>
      </header>
      <ul class="next-links">
        <li><a href="/visa-categories.html"><strong>Review visa categories</strong><span>Orient the route before discussing scope.</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/official-tools.html"><strong>Check official tools</strong><span>Use the government source before accepting a summary.</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="/contacts.html"><strong>Draft the question brief</strong><span>Keep the first handoff concise and low-risk.</span></a></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="source-note">For current instructions, start with <a href="https://www.uscis.gov/" rel="noreferrer">USCIS</a>, the <a href="https://travel.state.gov/content/travel/en/us-visas.html" rel="noreferrer">Department of State</a>, or the school, sponsor, employer, or attorney responsible for your situation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .scope-intro {
    background: var(--color-navy);
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .scope-intro__grid {
    align-items: end;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.1fr) minmax(18rem, 0.9fr);
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
  }

  .scope-intro h1,
  .scope-intro h2 {
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .scope-intro h1 {
    max-width: 17ch;
  }

  .scope-intro .eyebrow {
    color: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .scope-intro__lede {
    color: var(--color-on-dark-muted);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2);
    max-width: 58ch;
  }

  .intro-actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-1);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
  }

  .scope-note {
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--color-gold);
    padding: var(--space-3);
  }

  .scope-note .eyebrow {
    margin-block-end: var(--space-1);
  }

  .scope-note h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    max-width: 19ch;
  }

  .scope-note p:last-child {
    color: var(--color-on-dark-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .section-heading,
  .scope-next > div > header {
    max-width: 56rem;
  }

  .section-heading h2,
  .payment-grid h2,
  .scope-faq h2,
  .scope-next h2 {
    max-width: 24ch;
  }

  .table-wrap {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  .scope-table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    min-width: 48rem;
    width: 100%;
  }

  caption {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-1);
    text-align: start;
  }

  th,
  td {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-1);
    text-align: start;
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  thead th {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line-dark);
    color: var(--color-soft);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  tbody th {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    width: 22%;
  }

  td {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .payment-grid,
  .scope-faq__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.72fr) minmax(0, 1.28fr);
  }

  .payment-grid > header,
  .scope-faq__grid > header {
    max-width: 32rem;
  }

  .payment-list,
  .next-links {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line-dark);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .payment-list li {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    grid-template-columns: 2.2rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
  }

  .payment-list li > span {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .payment-list strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .payment-list p {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    margin: 0.25rem 0 0;
  }

  .faq-list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line-dark);
  }

  .faq-list details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .faq-list summary {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    font-weight: 750;
    list-style: none;
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
  }

  .faq-list summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-list summary::after {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    content: '+';
    float: right;
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .faq-list details[open] summary::after {
    content: '–';
  }

  .faq-list details p {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    max-width: 62ch;
    padding-block-end: var(--space-2);
  }

  .scope-next {
    background: var(--color-paper);
  }

  .next-links {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
  }

  .next-links li {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .next-links a {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.3rem 1.5rem;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(12rem, 0.5fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .next-links strong {
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .next-links span,
  .source-note {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .source-note {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-3);
  }

  .source-note a {
    color: var(--color-accent-dark);
    font-weight: 750;
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .scope-intro__grid,
    .payment-grid,
    .scope-faq__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .scope-note {
      max-width: 38rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .intro-actions .button {
      width: 100%;
    }

    .next-links a {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
